<title>ITALY: Olivetti denies plans for capital increase.</title>
<headline>Olivetti denies plans for capital increase.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian information technology group Olivetti categorically denied that it was planning a capital increase, a company spokesman said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The Olivetti spokesman said that the company, &quot;denies categorically whatever the idea of a capital issue&quot;.</p>
<p>Olivetti shares declined 6.62 percent on Thursday due to market talk concerning a possible capital increase. The shares on Friday rose 2.92 percent to 582 lire by 0815 GMT in a firmer Milan stock market.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
